<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ meta.title }}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --ink: #1f2937;
      --muted: #5b6472;
      --line: #d8dee8;
      --paper: #ffffff;
      --wash: #f6f8fb;
      --accent: #1f6feb;
      --good: #0f766e;
      --bad: #b42318;
      --bayes: #7c3aed;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--wash);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: "Avenir Next", "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    main { max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
    h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0; }
    p { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
    .meta, .limitations { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .howto {
      background: #eef4ff;
      border: 1px solid #cfdcf7;
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
      margin: 1.2rem 0 2rem;
    }
    .key-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 0.6rem; }
    .key-table th, .key-table td {
      border-top: 1px solid #cfdcf7;
      padding: 0.45rem 0.5rem;
      text-align: left;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    .key-table th { color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .era { margin-top: 2.2rem; }
    .era-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
      padding-top: 0.8rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .era-head p { color: var(--muted); max-width: 62ch; }
    .card {
      background: var(--paper);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.2rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
    }
    .card-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }
    .verdict-chip {
      display: inline-block;
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .verdict-chip.ordinary { color: var(--good); background: #e6f4f1; }
    .verdict-chip.flagged { color: var(--bad); background: #fdecea; }
    .verdict-chip.bayesian { color: var(--bayes); background: #f1eafe; }
    .chart { margin: 0.5rem 0 0.9rem; overflow-x: auto; }
    .chart svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
    .explain {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-top: 0.6rem;
    }
    .explain div {
      background: var(--wash);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 0.7rem 0.75rem;
    }
    .explain strong {
      display: block;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }
    .verdict { border-left: 4px solid var(--line); padding-left: 0.8rem; margin-top: 0.8rem; }
    .verdict strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      .explain { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .era-head, .card-head { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; }
    }
    @media print {
      body { background: #fff; }
      .card { break-inside: avoid; box-shadow: none; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>{{ meta.title }}</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Generated {{ generated_at }} · Snapshot SHA256 {{ meta.snapshot_sha256 }} ·
    {{ meta.n_draws }} draws across {{ meta.n_eras }} eras.
  </p>

  <section class="howto">
    <h2>How to read this report</h2>
    <p>Each check gets one chart and three plain-English notes: what the plot shows, what fair output should look like, and what pattern would worry me. A quiet report means the checks found the ordinary amount of scatter expected once the number of checks is taken into account.</p>
  </section>

  {% if era_key %}
  <section class="howto">
    <h2>Era key</h2>
    <p>An era is a stretch of draws played under one set of rules. Eras are audited separately because changing the pool size or draw format changes what fair looks like.</p>
    <table class="key-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Era</th><th>Dates</th><th>Rules</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for era in era_key %}
        <tr><td>{{ era.name }}</td><td>{{ era.dates }}</td><td>{{ era.rules }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% for era in eras %}
  <section class="era">
    <div class="era-head">
      <h2>{{ era.name }}</h2>
      <p>{{ era.headline }}</p>
    </div>
    {% for family in era.families %}
    <article class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <h3>{{ family.title }}</h3>
        <span class="verdict-chip {{ family.status }}">{{ family.status }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chart">{{ family.svg | safe }}</div>
      <div class="explain">
        <div><strong>What this plot shows</strong>{{ family.shows }}</div>
        <div><strong>What fair looks like</strong>{{ family.fair }}</div>
        <div><strong>What would worry me</strong>{{ family.worry }}</div>
      </div>
      <p class="verdict"><strong>Verdict:</strong> {{ family.verdict }} {{ family.chance }}</p>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <section class="era">
    <div class="era-head">
      <h2>Power analysis</h2>
      <p>How often the planted test biases were detected, so a quiet report is meaningful only where the checks are powerful.</p>
    </div>
    <article class="card">
      {% if power_svg %}
      <div class="chart">{{ power_svg | safe }}</div>
      {% else %}
      <p>No power-analysis grid was supplied.</p>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="explain">
        <div><strong>What this plot shows</strong>The share of simulated biased lotteries that each check managed to catch.</div>
        <div><strong>What fair looks like</strong>Detection should rise as the planted bias gets stronger; weak checks can miss subtle bias.</div>
        <div><strong>What would worry me</strong>A clean real-data result next to a check that cannot detect the bias size we care about.</div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="limitations">
    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p>This audit tests the recorded draw data, not the physical machine. A pass means these checks found no convincing deviation in this snapshot; it is not a guarantee of future fairness.</p>
  </section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
